 Many tests need external binaries (svn, git, hg, bzr, cvs, ImageMagick, Ghostscript, Pandoc) or services (LDAP, Chrome for system tests); results vary by machine and some are silently skipped.\n- The git repository is a mirror of the upstream Subversion repository (commit messages cite rNNNNN; svn:ignore commits). Harness files added here may conflict with upstream syncs and are not accepted upstream.\n- Existing CI runs only on push and does not call a task runner; editing tests.yml or linters.yml could diverge from upstream.\n\n5:## Notes from the harness build\n15:## 2026-11-01: harness built by uw-harness 0.3.0 with claude","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019sSqaNPKNdHLBCMMXr5WYh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdgENHZR7M4L1aY4RGgL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CwwbumzfuC7GYYxbYtrz4M","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> docs/harness/log.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-11-02: warn when search terms of a text filter are truncated (#44464)\n\nText filters (string, text and search types) with an operator that splits the value into search terms (`~`, `*~`, `!~`, `^`, `$`) used only the first 5 terms, and the rest was dropped silently. `Redmine::Search::Tokenizer` now has `MAX_TOKENS = 5` and `truncated?`. `Query#filter_warnings` returns one message per truncated filter. The issue list, time entries (list and report), calendar and Gantt chart show the messages as `<p class=\"warning\">` above the results through `render_query_filter_warnings`. Warnings do not make the query invalid. Tests cover the tokenizer, the query model, the helper (escaping) and the four views. `check-fast` and `check` pass.\n\nWhat was learned: `$` (ends with) also splits the value into terms through `Query.tokenized_like_conditions`, so it is included with the operators listed in the issue. Only the first value of a filter is used by the SQL, so only that value is checked. The message key is `notice_query_search_terms_truncated` (next to the Gantt truncation notice). Other locales fall back to English.\n\nLeft: the issues report and the search page (`/search`) do not show the warning; the search page already shows its own tokens (`@tokens`).\nEOF\ngit diff --stat","description":"Append dated log entry and show diff stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2332,"cache_read_input_tokens":88067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2332},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6cec20ce-e37b-42cf-8d54-8a9c0abff5c9","uuid":"5a8cb2f9-a5d1-4a53-91e4-70a6eb77e869","timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:05:46.760Z","request_id":"req_011CgdgEMtVZmLkZ6RH4GZ7p","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CwwbumzfuC7GYYxbYtrz4M":{"command":"cd /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/bench/trees/redmine-2-harness-haiku && cat >> docs/harness/log.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-11-02: warn when search terms of a text filter are truncated (#44464)\n\nText filters (string, text and search types) with an operator that splits the value into search terms (`~`, `*~`, `!~`, `^`, `$`) used only the first 5 terms, and the rest was dropped silently. `Redmine::Search::Tokenizer` now has `MAX_TOKENS = 5` and `truncated?`. `Query#filter_warnings` returns one message per truncated filter. The issue list, time entries (list and report), calendar and Gantt chart show the messages as `<p class=\"warning\">` above the results through `render_query_filter_warnings`. Warnings do not make the query invalid. Tests cover the tokenizer, the query model, the helper (escaping) and the four views. `check-fast` and `check` pass.\n\nWhat was learned: `$` (ends with) also splits the value into terms through `Query.tokenized_like_conditions`, so it is included with the operators listed in the issue. Only the first value of a filter is used by the SQL, so only that value is checked. The message key is `notice_query_search_terms_truncated` (next to the Gantt truncation notice). Other locales fall back to English.\n\nLeft: the issues report and the search page (`/search`) do not show the warning; the search page already shows its own tokens (`@tokens`).\nEOF\ngit diff --stat","description":"Append dated log entry and show diff stat"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01CwwbumzfuC7GYYxbYtrz4M":{"cwd":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/redmine/bench/trees/redmine-2-harness-haiku"}}}
